1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,260
Weeks before his comeback, Michael Jackson was gone.

2
00:00:06,670 --> 00:00:10,920
This is what happened on the twenty fifth of June, 2009, and what a court

3
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:12,410
decided in November 2011.

4
00:00:15,830 --> 00:00:20,970
On 14 May 1984, President Ronald Reagan welcomed Michael Jackson to the White

5
00:00:21,010 --> 00:00:21,370
House.

6
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:25,500
Jackson had taken part in a campaign against drunk driving, and the President

7
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:26,480
honoured him for it.

8
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:30,360
Here is how the President introduced him, in his own words.

9
00:00:30,770 --> 00:00:37,430
No, I know why you're here, and with good reason, to see one of the most talented, most popular,

10
00:00:37,470 --> 00:00:40,730
and most exciting superstars in the music world today, Michael Jackson.

11
00:00:40,770 --> 00:00:45,230
Michael, welcome to the White House.

12
00:00:45,570 --> 00:00:49,270
Reagan then read out the text of an award, which he presented that morning.

13
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:59,660
To Michael Jackson, with appreciation for the outstanding example you have set for the youth of America and the world.

14
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:06,460
Your historic record-breaking achievements and your preeminence in popular music are a tribute to your creativity,

15
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:10,960
dedication, and great ability.

16
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:18,460
The generous contribution of your time and talent to the national campaign against teenage drunk driving

17
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:24,960
will help millions of young Americans learn that drinking and driving can kill a friendship.

18
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,720
Here is Jackson's reply on the South Lawn.

19
00:01:27,330 --> 00:01:29,290
I'm very, very honored.

20
00:01:29,330 --> 00:01:31,690
Thank you very much, Mr. President

21
00:01:31,730 --> 00:01:35,190
and Mrs. Reagan.

22
00:01:35,530 --> 00:01:38,690
That was twenty five years before the day this story is about.

23
00:01:39,100 --> 00:01:43,900
By 2009, Jackson was fifty years old, and he was planning a return to the

24
00:01:43,940 --> 00:01:44,300
stage.

25
00:01:44,730 --> 00:01:49,940
The plan was a run of fifty concerts at the O2 Arena in London, promoted by AEG

26
00:01:49,980 --> 00:01:50,270
Live.

27
00:01:50,700 --> 00:01:55,280
The first show was due to open on 13 July 2009.

28
00:01:55,700 --> 00:01:59,480
ABC News reported at the time that all fifty shows were sold out.

29
00:01:59,900 --> 00:02:04,240
The rehearsals were filmed, and ABC later reported more than a hundred hours

30
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:04,880
of footage.

31
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:09,660
On the morning of 25 June, opening night was eighteen days away.

32
00:02:13,070 --> 00:02:16,310
It was Thursday, 25 June 2009.

33
00:02:16,730 --> 00:02:20,950
At 12:21 in the afternoon, a call was made to the emergency number from a

34
00:02:20,990 --> 00:02:24,730
rented house in the Holmby Hills area, where Jackson was staying.

35
00:02:25,170 --> 00:02:28,790
He was taken to the UCLA Medical Center, a few minutes away.

36
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:32,120
He was declared dead at 2:26 in the afternoon.

37
00:02:32,530 --> 00:02:35,730
His brother Jermaine Jackson announced the death to reporters.

38
00:02:36,170 --> 00:02:38,690
News organisations tried to confirm it.

39
00:02:38,730 --> 00:02:43,170
CNN said the Los Angeles Times and CBS News were reporting his death.

40
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:47,860
The Register reported that American news websites struggled as readers rushed to

41
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:50,580
confirm the news, and that Twitter search crumpled.

42
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:55,290
As of eight that morning, the O2 Arena website was still advertising tickets

43
00:02:55,330 --> 00:02:56,620
for the comeback shows.

44
00:02:57,030 --> 00:03:01,350
Here is the moment CNN's live coverage reached the confirmation.

45
00:03:01,770 --> 00:03:04,330
I have to stop you for a second, A.J.

46
00:03:04,370 --> 00:03:07,530
CNN can now confirm from the LA coroner that Michael Jackson is dead.

47
00:03:07,870 --> 00:03:11,330
Helicopter pictures showed crowds gathering outside the hospital.

48
00:03:11,730 --> 00:03:15,190
His body was taken to the Los Angeles County Coroner's office.

49
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:17,600
The London shows did not go ahead.

50
00:03:18,030 --> 00:03:22,360
How he died would take two months to be named, and more than two years to be

51
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:23,350
decided in court.

52
00:03:26,770 --> 00:03:30,950
The first goodbye came on Tuesday, 7 July 2009.

53
00:03:31,370 --> 00:03:34,670
A public memorial was held at the Staples Center in Los Angeles.

54
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:39,220
Nielsen counted about thirty one million viewers in the United States alone.

55
00:03:39,630 --> 00:03:43,830
Musicians performed and friends spoke, and at the end, his daughter Paris, then

56
00:03:43,870 --> 00:03:45,510
eleven, came to the microphone.

57
00:03:45,930 --> 00:03:51,180
On Friday, 28 August 2009, the Los Angeles County Coroner released its

58
00:03:51,220 --> 00:03:51,870
findings.

59
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:55,100
The coroner ruled the manner of death a homicide.

60
00:03:55,530 --> 00:04:00,630
The cause was acute propofol intoxication, with the sedative

61
00:04:00,670 --> 00:04:04,370
lorazepam named as a contributing condition.

62
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:09,520
Propofol is a strong anaesthetic, used in hospitals during surgery.

63
00:04:09,930 --> 00:04:14,990
In a coroner's report, homicide means a death caused by the actions of another

64
00:04:15,030 --> 00:04:15,450
person.

65
00:04:15,490 --> 00:04:18,490
It is a classification, not a verdict of guilt.

66
00:04:18,900 --> 00:04:24,940
On 28 October 2009, a film made from the rehearsal footage opened in cinemas for

67
00:04:24,980 --> 00:04:26,100
a two week run.

68
00:04:26,530 --> 00:04:30,410
Its director, Kenny Ortega, called it Michael's gift to his fans.

69
00:04:30,830 --> 00:04:34,200
The question left open was whether anyone would answer for the death in

70
00:04:34,240 --> 00:04:34,490
court.

71
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:42,160
The man at the centre was Conrad Murray, a Houston cardiologist, and Jackson's

72
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:43,220
personal physician.

73
00:04:43,630 --> 00:04:48,470
Two days after the death, on 27 June 2009, Los Angeles police interviewed

74
00:04:48,510 --> 00:04:51,650
him, and the jury later heard a recording of it.

75
00:04:52,070 --> 00:04:56,290
Here is part of that recording, as played in court and aired by ABC News.

76
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:03,460
Murray's recorded police interview, played to the jury

77
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:08,900
On 8 February 2010, Murray was arraigned in Los Angeles on a charge of

78
00:05:08,940 --> 00:05:12,560
involuntary manslaughter, and he pleaded not guilty.

79
00:05:12,970 --> 00:05:18,290
His trial opened on 27 September 2011, and ran for about six weeks.

80
00:05:18,700 --> 00:05:22,420
Prosecutors said Murray failed to monitor his patient closely while

81
00:05:22,460 --> 00:05:26,300
Jackson was sedated, and pointed to phone calls he made that morning.

82
00:05:26,730 --> 00:05:29,900
Murray's lawyers said he met his professional duties.

83
00:05:29,940 --> 00:05:34,520
In court filings they suggested that Jackson may have given himself an extra

84
00:05:34,560 --> 00:05:34,830
dose.

85
00:05:35,270 --> 00:05:38,420
The jury reached a unanimous decision on a Monday.

86
00:05:38,460 --> 00:05:42,270
Reports put the deliberations at between nine and ten hours.

87
00:05:42,700 --> 00:05:48,000
On Monday, 7 November 2011, a Los Angeles jury found Conrad Murray guilty

88
00:05:48,040 --> 00:05:50,080
of involuntary manslaughter.

89
00:05:50,500 --> 00:05:54,630
Murray was taken into custody that day, and outside the courthouse, fans and

90
00:05:54,670 --> 00:05:56,360
protesters gathered with signs.

91
00:05:56,770 --> 00:05:59,030
Here is the verdict being read in the courtroom.

92
00:05:59,630 --> 00:06:02,790
We, the jury, in the above-entitled action,

93
00:06:02,830 --> 00:06:09,690
find the defendant, Conrad Robert Murray, guilty of the crime of involuntary manslaughter.

94
00:06:10,030 --> 00:06:13,170
Afterwards, the lead prosecutor spoke to reporters.

95
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:20,260
Our sympathies go out to the Jackson family at this time for the loss that they have suffered.

96
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:26,010
Three weeks later, on 29 November 2011, Judge Michael Pastor sentenced Murray to

97
00:06:26,050 --> 00:06:28,220
four years in jail, the maximum.

98
00:06:28,630 --> 00:06:33,030
The judge said Murray had shown no sense of remorse, and that Jackson died not

99
00:06:33,070 --> 00:06:37,190
from one isolated incident, but from a totality of circumstances directly

100
00:06:37,230 --> 00:06:38,510
attributable to Murray.

101
00:06:38,930 --> 00:06:43,180
Pastor rejected the idea of seeing Murray as either a saint or a devil.

102
00:06:43,220 --> 00:06:44,890
He called him a human being.

103
00:06:45,300 --> 00:06:49,410
The Jackson family told the court it was not seeking revenge, and asked for a

104
00:06:49,450 --> 00:06:53,500
sentence that would remind physicians they cannot sell their services to the

105
00:06:53,540 --> 00:06:54,320
highest bidder.

106
00:06:54,730 --> 00:06:59,050
Prosecutors had asked for one hundred million dollars in restitution.

107
00:06:59,090 --> 00:07:01,930
The judge left the amount for a later hearing.

108
00:07:02,370 --> 00:07:07,620
Under California law, Murray served about half of the sentence, and he was

109
00:07:07,660 --> 00:07:09,650
released on 28 October 2013.

110
00:07:10,070 --> 00:07:14,320
His attorney stressed that Murray had not been convicted of murder, but of

111
00:07:14,360 --> 00:07:15,790
involuntary manslaughter.

112
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:20,880
Texas revoked his medical licence in 2013, and California had suspended it

113
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:22,240
after the conviction.

114
00:07:22,670 --> 00:07:28,130
In a separate civil case, on 2 October 2013, a jury cleared the concert

115
00:07:28,170 --> 00:07:31,910
promoter AEG Live of negligence in hiring Murray.

116
00:07:32,330 --> 00:07:35,790
A win could have meant hundreds of millions of dollars in damages for

117
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:38,310
Katherine Jackson and the singer's three children.

118
00:07:38,730 --> 00:07:42,870
So one man was convicted in the criminal case, and the promoter was cleared in

119
00:07:42,910 --> 00:07:43,630
the civil one.
